Runtime data lives here, outside sites/ and pub/.

The formatter cache defaults to var/cache. Werc creates it with mode 0700 if
this directory is writable. Otherwise formatting works without caching.
For a CGI deployment, create var/cache owned by the CGI user with mode 0700.
Never put the cache in a shared writable directory or expose it through HTTP.
Set cache_root=() in etc/initrc.local to disable it. Remove cached files after
changing a formatter implementation or its options. Cache entries are derived
only from file contents; timestamp-preserving edits are detected.

Only pure filters are cached. Directory generators such as the sitemap run
fresh because their output also depends on configuration and request context.
